<MainLayout title="Main Sewer Line Cleaning Mason City IA | Sewer Clog" description="Main sewer line cleaning in Mason City, Iowa for whole-house backups, multiple slow drains, sewage backups and recurring sewer clogs."><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Main sewer line cleaning</p><h1>When the Main Sewer Line Backs Up</h1><p>If the toilet gurgles when the washer drains, several fixtures back up together, or sewage appears at the basement floor drain, the blockage may be in the main sewer line.</p><p><a class="btn" href="tel:6415302728">Call 641-530-2728</a></p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><h2>Signs of a Main Sewer Clog</h2><ul class="list"><li>Several drains slow down at once</li><li>Toilet backs up when another fixture runs</li><li>Basement floor drain fills with dirty water</li><li>Sewer odor appears around a drain</li><li>The line clears and plugs again</li></ul><h2>Why Repeat Clogs Matter</h2><p>A cable can open a blocked line, but repeated blockages can have an underlying cause such as tree roots, heavy buildup, damaged joints or another pipe problem. When the history of the line calls for it, a camera inspection can help locate the problem.</p></div></section></MainLayout>